<title>USA: Global Ocean Carriers sells 144a notes.</title>
<headline>Global Ocean Carriers sells 144a notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following 144a debt issue from Global Ocean Carriers Ltd was priced Thursday via lead</p>
<p>manager Lazard Freres &amp; Co, according to a market source.</p>
<p>BORROWER GLOBAL OCEAN CARRIERS LTD</p>
<p>AMT $126 MLN	 COUPON 10.25 PCT  MATURITY 7/15/2007</p>
<p>TYPE SNR NOTES     ISS PRICE 98.482  FIRST PAY DATE 1/15/1998</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S B2    YIELD 10.50 PCT   PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P B-PLUS    SPREAD +431 BPS   CALLABLE  NON-CALL FIVE</p>
<p>NOTES: The notes have a three-year equity call for 35 percent</p>
<p>of the issue at 110.25</p>
<p>((U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212-859-1678))</p>
</text>
